questions.explanation:
x<sup>2</sup> + x + 1 = 0


$$ \Rightarrow $$ x = $${{ - 1 + i\sqrt 3 } \over 2}$$ = $$\omega $$ or $${{ - 1 - i\sqrt 3 } \over 2}$$ = $${\omega ^2}$$


Let $$\alpha $$ = $$\omega $$


$$ \therefore $$ A = $${1 \over {\sqrt 3 }}\left[ {\matrix{
   1 &amp; 1 &amp; 1  \cr 
   1 &amp; \omega  &amp; {{\omega ^2}}  \cr 
   1 &amp; {{\omega ^2}} &amp; {{\omega ^4}}  \cr 

 } } \right]$$


A<sup>2</sup> = $${1 \over 3}\left[ {\matrix{
   3 &amp; 0 &amp; 0  \cr 
   0 &amp; 0 &amp; 3  \cr 
   0 &amp; 3 &amp; 0  \cr 

 } } \right]$$ = $$\left[ {\matrix{
   1 &amp; 0 &amp; 0  \cr 
   0 &amp; 0 &amp; 1  \cr 
   0 &amp; 1 &amp; 0  \cr 

 } } \right]$$


Now A<sup>4</sup> = $$\left[ {\matrix{
   1 &amp; 0 &amp; 0  \cr 
   0 &amp; 1 &amp; 0  \cr 
   0 &amp; 0 &amp; 1  \cr 

 } } \right]$$ = I


$$ \therefore $$ A<sup>31</sup> = A<sup>28</sup>A<sup>3</sup> = A<sup>3</sup>
